Energy Trading and Risk Management

Business Need
1.	Unstructured Requirements Capture: Requirements are captured in meeting notes and recordings, making consolidation slow and error prone.
2.	Requirements Mapping & Traceability: Business requirements must be accurately mapped to ETRM functional areas, priorities, and traceability artifacts such as RTM, BDD, and FUT.
3.	Structured ETRM System Evaluation: ETRM system selection requires structured evaluation across scope, functional fit, integration, and coverage.
4.	Decision Ready Insights & Visibility: Decision makers need clear, auditable views of coverage, gaps, risks, and recommendations for faster approval.
Solution
Agent based ETRM automation platform built on Azure App Service using modular AI agents to support RTM, BDD, FUT, and ETRM Selection workflows.
Unified ingestion and persistence layer leveraging Azure Blob Storage for files and Azure Cosmos DB for metadata, traceability, and normalized domain models.
Event driven processing pipeline using Azure Service Bus and Azure Functions to asynchronously perform OCR, speech to text, and semantic content extraction.
Semantic indexing and retrieval layer implemented with Azure AI Search and vector embeddings to ground agent reasoning on extracted requirements.
Deterministic scoring and recommendation engine implemented in Python, combining hard constraint filtering with weighted multi criteria vendor evaluation logic.
Controlled Azure OpenAI integration used strictly for reasoning, summarization, and executive narrative generation—isolated from scoring and decision logic.
Benefits
<> Intelligent Requirement Extraction
<> Automated RTM, BDD & FUT Generation
<> Functional Coverage Visibility
<> Gaps & Risk Identification
<> Data Driven ETRM Shortlisting
<> Transparent Decision Rationale

